    <briefdescription>
<para>Helper struct to parse and store a memory address as base + index + offset. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>We ignore sign extensions when it is safe to do so. The following two expressions are not equivalent. To differentiate we need to store whether there was a sign extension involved in the index computation. (load (i64 add (i64 copyfromreg c) (i64 signextend (add (i8 load index) (i8 1)))) vs</para>
<para>(load (i64 add (i64 copyfromreg c) (i64 signextend (i32 add (i32 signextend (i8 load index)) (i32 1))))) </para>
    </detaileddescription>
